<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28635" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnăpĭi</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m.
		plur. (Mĕnapis for Menapiis, <i><span class="en">Mart. 13,
		54</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				people of Belgic Gaul, between the Meuse and the Scheldt</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Caes.
				B. G. 2, 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 4, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 17,
				31, § 106</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 4,
			28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			749</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnăpĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the chief town of
				the Menapii</i>, <i><span class="en">Aur. Vict. Caes. 39</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnăpĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to the Menapii</i>, Edict. Diocl. p. 14.</div>
